  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "2586-root",
    "title": "Professor Stephane Pradines' Talk on Ethiopian Mosques at INTBAU",
    "subtitle": "The Case of Nora and Islamic Architecture in the Region",
    "summary": "Watch Professor Stephane Pradines talk about Ethiopian mosques and Islamic architectures.",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "a0ebf82b6b695a36",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "2586-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/2586-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "Professor Stephane Pradines' Talk on Ethiopian Mosques at INTBAU"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "As part of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "INTBAU",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://www.intbau.org/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Ethiopia's online series, "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Professor Stephane Pradines",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "http://www.aku.edu/ismc/people/Pages/stephane-pradines.aspx",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "linktype": "url",
                    "uuid": null,
                    "anchor": null,
                    "custom": {}
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " delivered a talk on \"Ethiopian Mosques: The Case of Nora and Islamic Architecture in the Region\" on 18 March 2021."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Stephane Pradines, who is an archaeologist and Professor of Islamic Art and Architecture at AKU-ISMC, discussed his research and publication on the archaeological excavations from 2008 at the great mosque of Nora. Located in the Shoa Region, the town of Nora is situated midway between the high plateau and the flood plain of the River Awash and Northern Somalia. The research undertaken later helped to identify a style of mosque called the 'Adal' style or the mosque of Bilad al-Barbar, typically characterised by dry-stone masonry bonded together with an earth-based mortar with a very basic mihrab and a staircase minaret. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Organiser",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "bold"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The International Network for Traditional Building, Architecture and Urbanism (INTBAU) is an international organisation established in 2001 and works under the patronage of the founder, HRH The Prince of Wales. "
            }
          ]
        },
        {
